  "title": "RTPS: Move clamping the domain ID before a multiplication",
  "description": "The domain ID is sent as a 32-bit unsigned integer across the wire in\nRTPS, but the port mapping used limits it to around 230 values.\nMove clamping it into the valid range before it is multiplied by a\nconstant 250, which prevents the possibility of overflow on fuzzed\ndata.\n\nOSS Fuzz 509055566\n\n(Triggering this requires running the fuzzer with the option -runs=2\nor more.)\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
